# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF. Without this, a clone on a
# Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true rewrites shell scripts with CRLF, and
# the Linux CI container then fails them with a bare `bad interpreter` error
# that points nowhere near the cause.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST be LF regardless of any local git configuration, because
# something other than git parses them.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# PowerShell reads LF-terminated scripts without complaint, so *.ps1 stays on
# the repository-wide LF policy above. A CRLF exception here would be rewritten
# on every commit by the mixed-line-ending pre-commit hook (--fix=lf), leaving
# the two configurations permanently fighting over the same file.
#
# Add a CRLF exception only for formats that genuinely require it — *.bat and
# *.cmd, which cmd.exe will not parse with LF endings.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary — never diffed, never converted.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.parquet   binary
*.duckdb    binary

# Generated: collapse in diffs and exclude from language statistics, but still
# reviewable on demand.
poetry.lock linguist-generated=true -diff
